+{ PATCH: ground-truth RNG replacement for bare (zero-arg) Random -- NOT named
+  Random itself. Confirmed by direct compile (fpc -Mtp -CfSSE2 runworld.pas):
+  declaring a zero-arg Random here shadows fpc's *one-arg* Random(N) builtin
+  too for every unit that USES Int, breaking ATTACK.PAS:1497's own
+  Random(1) ("Wrong number of parameters specified") -- build-all-units.ps1's
+  standalone-per-unit compile doesn't catch this (it never links ATTACK.PAS
+  against a real caller of the shadowed symbol), only a real runworld.pas
+  build does. So this gets its own name instead, and only the one real call
+  site that needs it (NPE04.PAS's own NewBSRKBaseTarget, see NPE04.PAS.patch)
+  is edited to call it -- not a blanket redirect of every bare-Random call
+  site in the source tree (NPEINTR.PAS's GetNewDesignation/DeployXxxFleet
+  rolls, INTRFACE.PAS's efficiency formula) the way Rnd's redirect is,
+  since none of those are reachable from any golden domain yet either.
+  Draws from the same GroundTruthNextU32 stream Rnd uses, matching its C#
+  twin (GroundTruthRandom.NextDouble). Declared Double, not Real: -Mtp's Real
+  is lower-precision than IEEE double -- confirmed by a real divergence in
+  the groundtruthrng golden file's own reals= field, first showing up around
+  the 8th significant digit, when this was Real. GroundTruthRandom's own C#
+  double carries more precision than Real can hold. This function is a
+  test-only harness addition, not a real Pascal formula this port needs to
+  reproduce bit-for-bit, so there's no "real Real" behavior worth preserving
+  here -- Double is simply the correct choice for a value both sides need to
+  agree on exactly. }
+FUNCTION GroundTruthRandomReal: Double;
+
 IMPLEMENTATION
 
+{ PATCH: see GroundTruthSeed's own doc comment above. LCG constants
+  (1664525, 1013904223) are the Numerical Recipes parameters -- chosen for
+  simplicity/mutual comprehensibility (this project controls both
+  implementations, so they only need to agree with each other, not be
+  statistically strong), and because they stay within LongWord/32-bit
+  wraparound arithmetic this whole codebase already trusts, no new-width
+  risk. }
+FUNCTION GroundTruthNextU32: LongWord;
+   BEGIN
+   GroundTruthSeed:=GroundTruthSeed*1664525+1013904223;
+   GroundTruthNextU32:=GroundTruthSeed;
+   END;  { GroundTruthNextU32 }
+
+{ PATCH: see this function's own INTERFACE doc comment. }
+FUNCTION GroundTruthRandomReal: Double;
+   VAR
+      Draw: Double;
+   BEGIN
+   Draw:=GroundTruthNextU32;
+   GroundTruthRandomReal:=Draw/4294967296.0;
+   END;  { GroundTruthRandomReal }
